    <div id="introduction-to-online-accessible-bluff">
        <b>Introduction to Online Accessible-Bluff</b><br><br>
        Games play a crucial role in human life; they help in improving concentration, skill development, social interaction, memory, teamwork, and creativity.
        However, visually impaired individuals have limited gaming options. Accessible Bluff is an inclusive online card game designed to be played seamlessly by all users.
    </div><br>

    <div id="how-to-play-bluff">
        <b>How to play bluff game?</b><br><br>
        Players gather, shuffle the deck, and take turns placing cards while either telling the truth or bluffing. Others can challenge the move.
        If a challenge succeeds, the bluffer is penalized. If the challenge fails, the challenger is penalized. The game continues until one player has no cards left.
    </div><br>

    <div id="how-to-play-online-accessible-bluff">
        <b>How to Play Online Accessible-Bluff?</b><br><br>
        Accessible Bluff supports screen readers, allowing visually challenged players to navigate the game. The process begins with Google login and profile setup.
        Players can create or join a room, and the game starts once all players have joined. The player who initiates the round chooses the bluff text. 
        Rounds continue until a winner emerges.
    </div><br>

    <div id="home-page-options">
        <b>Home Page Options</b><br><br>
        1. Account: Access profile details.<br>
        2. About: Learn about the application.<br>
        3. User guide: Instructions for using the game.<br>
        4. Log out: Exit the application.<br>
    </div><br>

    <div id="winning-criteria">
        <b>Winning Criteria</b><br><br>
        1. The player who gets rid of all cards wins.<br>
        2. If all but one player are eliminated, the remaining player wins.<br>
        3. If all players are blacklisted except one, the last remaining player wins.<br>
    </div><br>

    <div id="round-changing-criteria">
        <b>Round Changing Criteria</b><br><br>
        1. If all players choose ‘Pass,’ the round ends.<br>
        2. If a player challenges a bluff, the penalized player starts the next round.<br>
    </div><br>

    <div id="competency-criteria">
        <b>Competency Criteria</b><br><br>
        Competency is assessed after 11 games and displayed in the Competency Profile.<br>
        - Expert: 76-100 marks<br>
        - Excellent: 51-75 marks<br>
        - Very Good: 26-50 marks<br>
        - Good: 0-25 marks<br>
    </div><br>

